us="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ETO, YOSHIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUZAKI, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>To prevent the brazing material on the surface of a header pipe from entering the inside of a through hole when a connection block for connection of a liquid tank is brazed in a furnace to the header pipe, pipe-shaped projections are formed on the header pipe connection side of a pair of through holes which are formed in the connection block for connection of the liquid tank and through which the refrigerant enters and exits, the projections are inserted into the holes of the header pipe cladded with brazing material, and it is integrally fused with the capacitor.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Pour empêcher la brasure sur la surface d'un tube collecteur de pénétrer à l'intérieur d'un trou traversant lors du soudage d'un bloc de raccordement pour le branchement d'un réservoir de liquide dans une chaudière conduisant à un tube collecteur, on réalise des saillies en forme de tuyau sur le côté branchement (tube collecteur) d'une paire de trous traversants percés dans le bloc de raccordement du réservoir de liquide par lesquels entre et sort le liquide de refroidissement. Ces saillies sont introduites dans les trous du tube de tête recouvert de brasure et sont fixées par fusion sur le condensateur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to